  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Create, upgrade or align ScaleDock product, library and tooling repos against one standard: the latest Node that Vercel supports, latest pnpm and the stable native TypeScript compiler, a strict Turborepo workspace, Next.js surfaces or a universal Expo app, an optional native-only Expo mobile app with PowerSync for offline data, Supabase with better-supabase (a local project per worktree or agent on the native runtime, and declarative schemas on pg-delta), Stripe Data Pipeline for billing reads, PermDock, an oRPC contract shared by the API, MCP and CLI, Fumadocs, and Vercel-first infrastructure (Vercel Flags, Workflow SDK 5, the Run SDK and Sandbox with Drives, Connect for third-party tokens, and Services with bindings). AI features use AI SDK 7 through AI Gateway, with `WorkflowAgent` for long runs, declared tool approvals and shadcn AI Elements; Next.js 16.4 routes guard their static output with `ensureStatic`. Lint and format run on Ultracite 8 over Oxlint and Oxfmt with type-aware rules at error, CI pins third-party actions to commit SHAs, runs the cheap gates as parallel steps in one job and the heavy ones as separate jobs, saves caches only from the default branch, scopes cache access with cache-mode, and runs zizmor on public repos, Valibot covers every schema, and Temporal is the one date library. Runs record bundle, type and CLI-startup baselines before and after, agent routes are cached, and every adapter shares one naming scheme that a drift test enforces. Agents verify Next.js work through the dev server's MCP endpoint and keep the tool-managed AGENTS.md blocks committed. Upgrade and align modes fill a gap table from a fixed checklist with a fixed status vocabulary, and every run ends with a report template; every version is looked up at run time. SKILL.md holds the inputs, ground rules, workflow and final checklist, and each area of the standard lives in its own reference so the agent loads only what the repo kind and selected surfaces need.",
